  "consumedSurfaceDispositions": [
    {
      "surface": "codex app-server stdio JSON-RPC methods consumed by the resident adapter",
      "difference": "The resident adapter speaks initialize, initialized, thread/start, thread/resume, thread/unsubscribe, turn/start, turn/interrupt, and turn/completed on one stdio process per binding. Exec argv is not consumed.",
      "disposition": "compatible"
    },
    {
      "surface": "MCP streamable HTTP credential field",
      "difference": "bearer_token fails configuration load for streamable_http on this pin. The adapter sends the capability credential in mcp_servers.*.http_headers.Authorization and does not use bearer_token or bearer_token_env_var.",
      "disposition": "adapted"
    },
    {
      "surface": "model provider credential field",
      "difference": "The inference loopback credential is model_providers.openkit-worker-inference.experimental_bearer_token with wire_api responses and requires_openai_auth false. env_key and OPENAI_API_KEY are not used.",
      "disposition": "adapted"
    },
    {
      "surface": "native permission decision because reject_once is absent",
      "difference": "AskForApproval includes never and SandboxMode includes danger-full-access. Unexpected command/file requests receive accept by default; elicitation receives accept, and item/permissions/requestApproval receives the requested permissions with scope turn. Offered refusal-only options retain reject_once or cancel for future policy.",
      "disposition": "adapted"
    },
    {
      "surface": "rollout cli_version consumed by provenance capture",
      "difference": "Capture trusts rollout session_meta payload.cli_version only when it equals the cli_version passed to CodexRuntimeCapture.create. Historical fixtures pass 0.153.4. The resident adapter passes 0.166.0. There is no default.",
      "disposition": "compatible"
    },
    {
      "surface": "one app-server process per binding",
      "difference": "Shared-host isolation is not proved. Each binding spawns and closes its own codex app-server process. thread/unsubscribe is used once, on the first Turn of a resumed binding, to apply that Turn's MCP servers and working directory.",
      "disposition": "compatible"
    },
    {
      "surface": "MCP supply change between Turns",
      "difference": "Codex lists MCP tools when the thread is loaded and does not list them again at turn/start. A new conversation binds them in thread/start. A resumed open proves the id first, then applies the first Turn's MCP servers and working directory once. A later change is rejected and is a successor AgentSession. config/mcpServer/reload and config/batchWrite are not used.",
      "disposition": "adapted"
    },
    {
      "surface": "unknown logical model without a catalog descriptor",
      "difference": "This pin accepts a logical model that has no model metadata and does not require a model catalog under CODEX_HOME. The adapter does not write a catalog.",
      "disposition": "compatible"
    },
    {
      "surface": "plugin and hook startup",
      "difference": "The adapter writes no base configuration. Native plugins and hooks load under authored configuration and trust; invocation disables update checks and web_search_request and selects ephemeral auth storage. Protected Turn overlays remain applied by the resident adapter.",
      "disposition": "compatible"
    },
    {
      "surface": "0.160.0 to 0.166.0 consumed App Server requests and notifications",
      "difference": "The 321-schema snapshot preserves consumed request fields, required turn/start fields, ThreadItem type discriminants, TurnStatus and permission enums. ThreadItem gains optional lifecycle timestamps, subAgentActivity model/reasoningEffort and imageGeneration generationId/inputImages; imageGeneration.result is removed and is not consumed. New thread prediction/read-state notifications are ignored by the existing notification selector.",
      "disposition": "compatible"
    },
    {
      "surface": "native assistant phases, errors and response items",
      "difference": "MessagePhase adds partial_answer. The adapter excludes commentary and partial_answer before final candidate counting, retaining rejection of multiple final answers. CodexErrorInfo changes from oneOf to extensible anyOf and adds modelNotFound/policyCapacityUnavailable; existing error handling retains generic failure and only specializes contextWindowExceeded. Raw response items gain optional encrypted/status fields and additional_tools; structural capture tolerates additions while retaining close refuses unqualified non-message history.",
      "disposition": "adapted"
    },
    {
      "surface": "unused removed protocol surface",
      "difference": "ModelProviderCapabilitiesReadResponse removes namespaceTools and ReviewDelivery removes detached. The adapter consumes neither removed surface. Additional account, requirements, hook, skill, feedback, attachment, usage and realtime schemas do not change an existing request.",
      "disposition": "compatible"
    },
    {
      "surface": "host-managed ChatGPT account boundary for the separate credential-delivery owner",
      "difference": "account/login/start type chatgptAuthTokens, server request account/chatgptAuthTokens/refresh, account/rateLimits/read and notification account/rateLimits/updated are present. Login and refresh schemas are unchanged from 0.160.0; account plans add sci/sci_plus. This snapshot upgrade does not implement credential delivery.",
      "disposition": "compatible"
    },
    {
      "surface": "native process/thread model-provider selection enforcement",
      "difference": "The pin rejects turn/start when the process provider differs from the thread provider and returns ModelProviderError data. The process now selects the existing openkit-worker-inference provider and declares its non-secret name, responses wire API and requires_openai_auth=false at launch. Its actual loopback endpoint and bearer remain in the existing thread-local in-memory overlay. No provider mismatch bypass, retry or fallback is added.",
      "disposition": "adapted"
    },
    {
      "surface": "0.166.0 native Responses metadata header projection",
      "difference": "Canonical body metadata retains tool_namespaces_info while the direct header omits it. The reader compares every decoded field after excluding only that body inventory, independently bounds both encoded strings to 16 KiB, and returns only normalized lineage and request phase.",
      "disposition": "adapted"
    },
    {
      "surface": "0.166.0 native additional-tools transport identity",
      "difference": "The deterministic client prefix uses canonical at_UUIDv5; native context items assigned an absent id use at_UUIDv7. Gateway admission requires either exact lowercase UUID version with RFC variant, preserves the identity only in provider input, and grants no authority, timestamp or durable continuity meaning.",
      "disposition": "adapted"
    },
    {
      "surface": "explicit plugin hook fixture approval",
      "difference": "Native hooks/list currentHash joins declaration/content hashes. The authored native test fixture stores trusted_hash and trusted_content_hash separately, matching the pinned trust owner. Production does not synthesize trust or alter retained configuration.",
      "disposition": "adapted"
    },
    {
      "surface": "0.166.0 native compaction history declarations",
      "difference": "Native compaction retains the ordinary Turn additional-tools history declaration and omits top-level tools. Gateway Provider projection preserves those declarations exactly. The native compactor drains output without the ordinary Tool executor. The independent regression follows this representation and retains history pairing, phase, refusal, no-replay and original-bound checks; it does not add a Gateway stripping boundary.",
      "disposition": "adapted"
    }
  ],
